/F1 18 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 770 Tm (The Power Within: What Charles Haanel's Foreword) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 748 Tm (Reveals About Changing Your Life) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 714 Tm (The forgotten inner force that can transform the way you think,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 695 Tm (act and live) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 661 Tm (What if the greatest difference between success and failure is not your circumstances,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 646 Tm (your background or your physical ability? What if it begins with the way you think? In) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 631 Tm (the foreword to The Master Key System, Charles Francis Haanel presents a powerful idea:) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 616 Tm (the mind is the creative force behind human progress. Some people appear to move towards) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 601 Tm (success with confidence and clarity. Others struggle for years to achieve the same) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 586 Tm (ambitions. Some give up before they begin. Haanel asks us to consider why this happens.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 571 Tm (His answer is that the most important difference is mental.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 548 Tm (The power that already exists within you) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 514 Tm (Haanel's foreword suggests that people often look outside themselves for the source of) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 499 Tm (their strength. They may wait for the right person, the right opportunity, better) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 484 Tm (circumstances or external approval before taking action. But his central message is that) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 469 Tm (power comes from within. When a person begins to recognise their own ability to think,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 454 Tm (choose and act deliberately, something important changes. They stop seeing themselves as) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 439 Tm (completely dependent on outside conditions. They begin to take responsibility for the) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 424 Tm (direction of their thoughts, their actions and their life. This does not mean that) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 409 Tm (external circumstances are irrelevant. Life contains genuine difficulties and challenges.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 394 Tm (It means that our inner response to those circumstances can influence the decisions we) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 379 Tm (make and the possibilities we are able to see.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 356 Tm (Why thought must be applied) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 322 Tm (Haanel does not present thought as a vague form of positive thinking. The foreword) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 307 Tm (repeatedly connects mental power with: Proper application. Diligence. Concentration.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 292 Tm (Understanding. Practice. Definite principles. This is important. Simply reading about) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 277 Tm (personal development is not the same as developing yourself. A person can read dozens of) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 262 Tm (books, listen to countless lectures and collect endless information without creating) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 247 Tm (meaningful change. Knowledge begins to become powerful when it is applied. The real) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 232 Tm (question is not only: What do I know? The deeper question is: What am I practising) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 217 Tm (consistently?) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 34 Tm (Unleash Your Power with Tariq - 1 / 4) Tj
ET
