BT
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 770 Tm (Your thoughts can create direction-or confusion) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 736 Tm (The foreword explains that the mind can contribute to favourable conditions, but it can) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 721 Tm (also reinforce negative conditions. When people repeatedly imagine lack, limitation, fear) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 706 Tm (and discord, these thoughts can influence the way they see their lives and respond to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 691 Tm (their circumstances. This does not mean that a person is responsible for every difficult) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 676 Tm (event that happens to them. It means that repeated patterns of thought can affect: What) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 661 Tm (they notice. What they believe is possible. How they interpret setbacks. Which) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 646 Tm (opportunities they recognise. How confidently they take action. The people and) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 631 Tm (environments they move towards. A person who constantly expects failure may ignore) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 616 Tm (opportunities that are directly in front of them. A person who begins developing courage,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 601 Tm (clarity and concentration may start noticing possibilities that were previously hidden by) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 586 Tm (fear or confusion.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 563 Tm (The law of cause and effect) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 529 Tm (One of the main themes in Haanel's foreword is the relationship between cause and effect.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 514 Tm (The scientific method seeks to understand why things happen. When a desired result is) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 499 Tm (identified, the next step is to discover the conditions that produce it. Haanel applies) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 484 Tm (this idea to personal development. If someone wants greater concentration, they need to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 469 Tm (practise concentration. If someone wants more clarity, they need to examine their) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 454 Tm (thinking and reduce mental confusion. If someone wants to become more disciplined, they) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 439 Tm (need to develop a daily practice that requires discipline. A result does not appear) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 424 Tm (simply because it is desired. It develops through the repeated conditions that support) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 409 Tm (it.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 386 Tm (The importance of concentration) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 352 Tm (Concentration is one of the most important ideas in the foreword. Without concentration,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 337 Tm (thought becomes scattered. A person may want success, health, confidence, peace and) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 322 Tm (financial security, but if their attention moves constantly from one fear to another,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 307 Tm (their mental energy becomes divided. Concentration means learning to direct attention) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 292 Tm (towards one chosen idea or purpose. This requires practice. You may sit quietly and) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 277 Tm (discover that your mind moves constantly. You may attempt to focus and find yourself) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 262 Tm (thinking about yesterday, tomorrow, unfinished tasks or imagined problems. This does not) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 247 Tm (mean you have failed. It means you have discovered the condition of your attention. Each) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 232 Tm (time you notice that your mind has wandered and calmly return it to your chosen subject,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 217 Tm (you are practising concentration.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 34 Tm (Unleash Your Power with Tariq - 2 / 4) Tj
