/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 770 Tm (The Master Key is not a promise of something for nothing) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 736 Tm (The foreword makes an important distinction. It presents The Master Key System as a study) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 721 Tm (of mental principles, not as magic or a shortcut to instant results. The message is not) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 706 Tm (that something can be gained without effort. Instead, the student is encouraged to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 691 Tm (understand the principles and apply them consistently. This is what makes the system) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 676 Tm (practical. It asks the student to: Study an idea. Understand its meaning. Practise it) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 661 Tm (repeatedly. Observe the results. Refine their application. Continue with greater) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 646 Tm (awareness. The value is found in the application.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 623 Tm (Developing the qualities within you) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 589 Tm (According to the foreword, the study of mental principles can help develop qualities such) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 574 Tm (as: Greater energy. Discernment. Mental flexibility. Stronger reasoning. Better memory.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 559 Tm (Initiative. Persistence. Wisdom in decision-making. Imagination. Definite desire.) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 544 Tm (Intelligent sympathy. A greater appreciation of life. These qualities are not developed) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 529 Tm (by wishing for them. They develop through repeated thought and action. A person becomes) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 514 Tm (more courageous by repeatedly choosing courage. A person becomes more disciplined by) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 499 Tm (repeatedly acting with discipline. A person becomes more focused by repeatedly returning) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 484 Tm (their attention to what matters.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 461 Tm (From fear and limitation to courage and possibility) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 427 Tm (One of the most powerful passages in the foreword describes replacing thoughts of) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 412 Tm (failure, despair, lack, limitation and discord with thoughts of courage, power,) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 397 Tm (inspiration and harmony. This should not be misunderstood as pretending that problems do) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 382 Tm (not exist. The practice is not to deny difficulty. It is to stop allowing difficulty to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 367 Tm (become the only thing you can see. When a person repeatedly gives attention to fear, fear) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 352 Tm (can dominate their decisions. When a person begins giving attention to courage, purpose) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 337 Tm (and constructive action, their choices can begin to change. They may become more willing) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 322 Tm (to communicate, learn, take responsibility, ask for help, pursue an opportunity or begin) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 307 Tm (again after a setback. This is how inner change can begin influencing outer behaviour.) Tj
/F1 15 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 284 Tm (Questions are searchlights) Tj
/F1 10.5 Tf
1 0 0 1 58 250 Tm (The foreword describes questions as powerful tools in the search for understanding. This) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 235 Tm (is a useful idea for anyone beginning a personal-development journey. Good questions) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 220 Tm (direct attention. Instead of asking: Why does everything always go wrong for me? You) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 205 Tm (might ask: What can I learn from this situation? Instead of asking: Why am I unable to) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 190 Tm (change? You might ask: What small action can I repeat today? Instead of asking: What is) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 175 Tm (missing from my life? You might ask: What ability do I need to develop next? The quality) Tj
1 0 0 1 58 160 Tm (of your questions can influence the direction of your thinking.) Tj
/F1 9 Tf 1 0 0 1 58 34 Tm (Unleash Your Power with Tariq - 3 / 4) Tj
